From 355d7d344e5a4c1856da6bc683faae3b1db647af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c <a@b>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:33:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] g4tools: only take the HDF5 1.6 code path on HDF5 1.x

The guard bounds the minor version but not the major one, so HDF5 2.x
(H5_VERS_MAJOR=2, H5_VERS_MINOR=2) satisfies (H5_VERS_MAJOR>=1) &&
(H5_VERS_MINOR<=6) and wrongly takes the HDF5 1.6 branch. There the
unversioned H5Gopen/H5Dopen/H5Gcreate/H5Acreate/H5Dcreate map to the
three-argument *2 functions, so every call site fails to compile with
"too few arguments to function 'hid_t H5Gopen2(hid_t, const char*, hid_t)'".

That branch also aliases toolx_H5free_memory to plain free(), releasing
HDF5-allocated memory without H5free_memory().

HDF5 2.x still ships the deprecated v1 API, so the existing else branch
compiles against it unchanged.
---
 source/externals/g4tools/include/toolx/hdf5/hdf5_h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/externals/g4tools/include/toolx/hdf5/hdf5_h b/source/externals/g4tools/include/toolx/hdf5/hdf5_h
index 9b6fd88..33bfd7c 100644
--- a/source/externals/g4tools/include/toolx/hdf5/hdf5_h
+++ b/source/externals/g4tools/include/toolx/hdf5/hdf5_h
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <hdf5.h>
 
-#if (H5_VERS_MAJOR>=1) && (H5_VERS_MINOR<=6)
+#if (H5_VERS_MAJOR==1) && (H5_VERS_MINOR<=6)
 #define toolx_H5Dopen           H5Dopen
 #define toolx_H5Dcreate         H5Dcreate
 #define toolx_H5Acreate         H5Acreate
-- 
2.55.0

